  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing rural access to food and livelihood security in small Bo chiefdom, Kenema district</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will be implemented in eight communities of small Bo Kenema district to contribute to CAFOD&#x2019;s Food and livelihood security and Emergency preparedness, response and recovery programme framework.  It is also designed in line with the Sierra Leone Presidents&#x2019; recovery priorities, which is a 24 months&#x2019; plan that includes Agriculture and Emergency preparedness as key sectors under its post Ebola recovery strategy.  
Caritas Kenema is implementing this project in collaboration with other appropriate line ministries i.e. MAFFs, MSWGCAs and local council heads. The project will target not only vulnerable groups (women and youths) but also rural communities that were heavily affected by the Ebola outbreak.</narrative>
  </description>
